  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Oils</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because the applicant has requested to prematurely terminate the project.The applicant Hanegraaf B.V., the Netherlands, and the local partner Cumacor 189 Pty Ltd, South Africa, will form a joint venture to produce semi-finished, 100% natural oils with a cosmetic grade, and to sell the oils to the cosmetic industry. The type of oils to be produced are Macula, Moringa and Macadamia oil, all produced from the nuts from these trees. The processing unit which will have a production capacity of about 30,000 litres annually will be located near Alldays, Limpopo, South Africa next to the location of an existing (former) PSI project.In sourcing the raw material, African Oil wants to involve local suppliers and local communities, but will also establish an own plantation. The project will lead to increased employment and income for people from all levels of education and thus will boost the local economy. The intention is that outgrowers will supply organically produced nuts to African Oil to enable the product be certified as organic.African Oil will reduce its carbon footprint by using solar energy, reducing the use of office paper and by planting carbon-fixing Spekboom trees.</narrative>
  </description>
